  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1030 PM MST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nTuesday through Wednesday... The upper level trough has progressed \nwell east of the region and will continue to move away from the \nCWA. Tuesday morning will remain chilly with lows dropping into \nthe mid 30s. Ridging will begin to move into the area tomorrow \nmorning meaning high pressure. This will create fair weather \nthrough Wednesday evening.\n\nThursday through Friday... Another upper level trough will begin to \nmove through the area Thursday through Friday. Models continue to \nplace the center of low pressure farther south in Mexico. Dry \nnorthwesterly winds will keep any moisture or any chance of \nprecipitation South of the CWA. Thursday evening zonal flow will \nbecome dominate on the backside of the trough creating fair weather \nfor the weekend.\n\nSaturday into Next Week... Zonal flow will continue from Friday into \nearly next week. Weather will be fair and dry with temperatures \nbecoming slightly above normal.",
